  "caption": "Quinn reached for the top-shelf biscuits and something under the ribs went click. After that, every twist in the car brought a sharp jab.\n\nA slipping rib happens when lower-rib cartilage shifts a little and irritates a nearby nerve. Scans are often normal, and the click usually isn't doing lasting damage.\n\nWhat can help: easing off twisting, bending and overhead triggers for a while, sleeping on the other side or hugging a pillow, trunk strength chosen to avoid the click, and gentle mobilisation or taping during flares.\n\nOther causes should be checked first. Chest pain with breathlessness, sweating or nausea needs 000. See a GP for fever, coughing blood, yellow skin, a swollen tender tummy, weight loss, a rash band, or pain after big trauma.\n\nOur Sydney CBD and Chatswood physios can help. Book via the link in bio.\n\nGeneral information only — not a substitute for an individual assessment.",
